                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4517b85c-7ce5-3f6f-b7cf-64b87349fcc2",
                        "entry_id": "de0ccdb1-f645-3b7b-8698-af632e45e869",
                        "glosses": [
                            "zusammenfassende Bezeichnung für alle zytologischen Strukturen, welche die innere Architektur der Zelle bestimmen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Zytologie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2057568b-8de6-45b1-81be-6219fc22aae5",
                                "sense_id": "4517b85c-7ce5-3f6f-b7cf-64b87349fcc2",
                                "text": "Das Zytoskelett wird hauptsächlich durch Proteinfilamente gebildet."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9163c4b8-f4fd-438d-aefe-bed167e23388",
                        "source_entry_id": "de0ccdb1-f645-3b7b-8698-af632e45e869",
                        "source_sense_id": "4517b85c-7ce5-3f6f-b7cf-64b87349fcc2",
                        "source_sense_description": "zytologische Strukturen, welche die innere Architektur der Zelle bestimmen",
                        "target_lang_word": "细胞骨架",
                        "target_lang_code": "zh",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0ca69f2d-6b65-4c53-9adc-432c48196180",
                        "source_entry_id": "de0ccdb1-f645-3b7b-8698-af632e45e869",
                        "source_sense_id": "4517b85c-7ce5-3f6f-b7cf-64b87349fcc2",
                        "source_sense_description": "zytologische Strukturen, welche die innere Architektur der Zelle bestimmen",
                        "target_lang_word": "cytoskeleton",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cytoskeleton",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "747e0104-2b63-323c-9af4-79c339c64952",
                                        "entry_id": "bebd2479-3a67-3526-989a-1657154a485c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A matrix of intercellular protein, in the forms of microfilaments and microtubules, that provide some rigidity to cells"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db77eca4-78e5-4dab-9a4b-e8a6acac1337",
                                                "sense_id": "747e0104-2b63-323c-9af4-79c339c64952",
                                                "text": "Thus, large systems such as viruses, multienzyme complexes, cell-cytoskeleta and flagella are usually constructed from multiple copies of the same protein."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62d7b98f-40ad-4ed3-912f-51af724af54c",
                                                "sense_id": "747e0104-2b63-323c-9af4-79c339c64952",
                                                "text": "Judged from Electron-Microscopy (EM) studies of bilayer depleted cytoskeleta the spectrin/actin network exhibits basically a hexagonal (triangular) topology."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94a42cec-628c-46cd-a60a-b5fbf879bf36",
                                                "sense_id": "747e0104-2b63-323c-9af4-79c339c64952",
                                                "text": "In this process, cellular debris and cytoskeleta of the lysed cells were effectively removed, and the underlying ECM remained intact and adhered to the entire area of the tissue culture dish."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2bbc5815-4df2-4aca-b1e0-0fc7628df716",
                                                "sense_id": "747e0104-2b63-323c-9af4-79c339c64952",
                                                "text": "Cells including leukocytes are not just bags of cytosol, but have structured cytoskeleta, surface structures, and different viscoelastic properties at different length and time scales."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6be528f7-ca2f-4b37-8f26-3784c4fbe859",
                                                "sense_id": "747e0104-2b63-323c-9af4-79c339c64952",
                                                "text": "One may consider then the resulting forms as due to the plasticity of organismal development, as cytoskeleta seem shaped, not just selected, also by gravity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dad41e7b-5a64-4f4c-a158-a5a48a5f1820",
                                                "sense_id": "747e0104-2b63-323c-9af4-79c339c64952",
                                                "text": "The Poisson distribution can model fiber-fiber contacts in random fiber networks. Biological examples include connective tissues (cartilage and tendons) and cellular cytoskeleta."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "64324308-f89d-4ba8-8ec9-6696768951e6",
                        "source_entry_id": "de0ccdb1-f645-3b7b-8698-af632e45e869",
                        "source_sense_id": "4517b85c-7ce5-3f6f-b7cf-64b87349fcc2",
                        "source_sense_description": "zytologische Strukturen, welche die innere Architektur der Zelle bestimmen",
                        "target_lang_word": "cytosquelette",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cytosquelette",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "07cd5f8b-dc60-3ae8-ace4-e9ef708fb882",
                                        "entry_id": "17bde647-f054-3234-a935-ece26dcb85e4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "L’ensemble organisé des polymères biologiques constituant le squelette de la cellule."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34237c57-7211-4c99-8513-a929718692aa",
                                                "sense_id": "07cd5f8b-dc60-3ae8-ace4-e9ef708fb882",
                                                "text": "Le cytosquelette est composé de trois types de filaments renouvelés constamment par polymérisation : l’actine, les microtubules et les filaments intermédiaires."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
